{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111608","id":2911088408,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6tg68Y","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111608","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111608.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111608.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111608","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111608/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111608/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111608/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/12e0158d3622ddd30ad34455b5f56ad41b603032","number":111608,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Enforce strict JSON for non-finite numbers, document native workaround","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Fixes #89777\r\n- Supersedes #111498\r\n- Depends on #111522\r\n\r\nConsider this my penance for kicking the hornet's nest with that premptive merge.\r\n\r\nIn trying to come up with a solution that would line up with the core team's specifications, I was looking into how various other implementations of JSON handle non-finite numbers. The one I ended up settling on is Javascript's, which turns the values into `null`. This is obviously not ideal, but JSON isn't an ideal standard so that checks out. Plus, it's more ideal than what we have now, as it follows what is arguably the most prevalent standard.\r\n\r\nHowever, because it's important to support transfering `INF`/`NAN` unambiguously through JSON by *some* means, this PR is dependent on the fix in #111522. This would allow these types to be converted to and from their native selves and JSON-safe string wrapper. This allows us to sidestep the rabbit hole of finding a \"correct\" way of representing these invalid types.\r\n\r\nTests and documentation have been expanded to account for this new behavior and the aforementioned workaround. This is also *technically* compatibility-breaking for the non-zero chance anyone was simultaneously relying on our invalid output **and** made a dedicated parser for the invalid output that we never supported, so it shouldn't be cherry-picked.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"no